Theorem VF-1: Verification layer signatures — VF-1 through VF-8

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS verification stack is layered, NOT a single function
      per Annex E §AIMS + arc.md sec-Verification-Surface
    - Each layer catches a different class of inconsistency; a fix that
      passes one layer but regresses another is a correctness regression
    - All VF rules have signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap x MemoryContract
      -> Bool per the canonical proof notation:285
    - VF-2 sub-checks (b), (c), (d) are target-only conditional on sec-08
      RL-29 / RL-30 / RL-31 LLVM fact export landing per Annex E §AIMS VF-2
    - 8 active VF theorems per the section inventory table (line 109)

  Soundness property:
    Common type signature for all VF rules (per the canonical proof notation:285):

      VF-N : ArcFunction x AimsStateMap x MemoryContract -> Bool

    VF-1 (Layer 1 — Structural well-formedness):
      type : ArcFunction -> Result () (List VerifyError)
      checks: UseBeforeDef, DanglingBlockRef, RcOnScalar, DecOnBorrowed
              (function-param restricted per Annex E §AIMS VF-1),
              ArgOwnershipLenMismatch
      three checkpoints: after AIMS emission (Step 6), after full pipeline
        (Step 11), after post-pipeline passes (sec-8 RL-22 through RL-26)

    VF-2 (Layer 2 — AIMS Contract Consistency):
      type : ArcFunction x AimsStateMap x MemoryContract -> Result () (List VerifyError)
      checks:
        (a) AbsentParamHasUses (parameters declared Absent MUST have no
            live uses on any forward-reachable path) — IMPLEMENTED
        (b) RL-31 alias metadata backed by disjointness proof — target-only
        (c) RL-29 noalias returns validated against ReturnContract —
            target-only
        (d) RL-30 memory(...) attributes derivable from IC-5 + parameter
            contracts — target-only
      Mandatory per VF-8 when shipped.

    VF-3 (Layer 3 — Oracle):
      type : ArcFunction -> MemoryContract
      re-derives MemoryContract from realized IR (the realized side of
      the contract); compares against inferred contract along access,
      consumption, effects dimensions; unsafe mismatches (analysis more
      optimistic than realization) = errors.

    VF-4 (Layer 4 — FIP Certification):
      type : ArcFunction x FipContract -> Result () (List FipVerificationError)
      proves FipContract::Certified functions have zero unmatched
      alloc / dealloc in realized IR; failures wrapped as
      VerifyError::FipStructural per pipeline runner wrap pattern.

    VF-5 (end-to-end verification mandate):
      type : Subsystem -> Bool
      every active subsystem SHALL be end-to-end verified: implementation
      + invariant enforcement + tests; missing any = incomplete.

    VF-6 (contracts-and-realization agreement):
      type : MemoryContract x ArcFunction -> Bool
      MemoryContract says FipContract::Certified -> realized IR has zero
      unmatched alloc / dealloc; analysis inferences match realized
      behavior (the realized-side check is what VF-3 oracle performs;
      VF-6 is the agreement invariant the verification stack as a whole
      enforces).

    VF-7 (active-rewrite three-tier discipline):
      type : Rewrite -> Bool
      every active rewrite (TRMC normalization, RL-22 through RL-26 post-
      pipeline RC motion) requires ALL THREE tiers:
        (a) compile-time structural verification (well-formedness,
            rollback on failure)
        (b) test-time behavioral verification (dedicated pre/post-rewrite
            test suites)
        (c) documented proof sketch (semantic preconditions where
            structural validity implies behavioral equivalence)
      Lacking any tier = not active.

    VF-8 (stack-applies-to-all-rules-incl-target-only):
      type : Rule -> Bool
      verification stack applies to ALL rules — incl. unimplemented sec-8
      rules + target-only sec-1.5 / IC-3 / IC-5 surface; unimplemented
      rule without verification layer planned = spec gap.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-09 verification-layer proofs
            (8 theorems: VF-1, VF-2, VF-3, VF-4, VF-5, VF-6, VF-7, VF-8)

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (VF-1 + VF-2 per-instruction structural-check
                            soundness)
      refinement (VF-3 oracle + VF-6 contracts-realization agreement)
      rc_counting (VF-4 FIP certification balance proof)
      interprocedural_summary (VF-2 (b) cross-call-site provenance summary
                               + VF-8 unimplemented-rule coverage check)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-09 discharges per-rule VF proofs
